OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1787080720
OL,3,CSalmonella outbreak: How can you check
OL,4,Cyour eggs are safe?
OL,6,FJacquelyn McCormick, Head of Incidents
OL,7,Fat the FSA, said eggs that are
OL,8,Fthoroughly cooked and handled
OL,9,Fhygienically should not present a food
OL,10,Fsafety risk.
OL,12,FIs there anything I should look out
OL,13,Ffor when buying eggs?
OL,15,FMs McCormick said: "Infants, young
OL,16,Fchildren, pregnant people and older
OL,17,Fadults should only eat runny or raw
OL,18,Feggs if they carry the British Lion
OL,19,Fmark or are produced under the Laid in
OL,20,FBritain egg assurance scheme."
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
